<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Deheubarth</h1><p class="st-meta">920 CE – 1197 CE (approx.) · capital Dinefwr</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of south-west Wales, founded by Hywel Dda and later led by the Lord Rhys, a centre of Welsh law, poetry and resistance to Norman conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Deheubarth, 'the southern part', was formed around 920 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hywel-dda">Hywel Dda</a> united his inheritance of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-seisyllwg">Kingdom of Seisyllwg</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dyfed">Dyfed</a>. Hywel later also ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Gwynedd</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-powys">Powys</a>, and became the only Welsh king to issue coins.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hywel was credited with codifying Welsh law, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyfraith-hywel">Cyfraith Hywel</a>, which governed inheritance, compensation and status. The kingdom's centre was Dinefwr in the Tywi valley. Norman lords overran much of it after 1093, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhys-ap-gruffydd">Rhys ap Gruffydd</a>, the Lord Rhys, rebuilt its power, held the first recorded eisteddfod at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardigan-wales">Cardigan</a> in 1176 and patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strata-florida-abbey">Strata Florida Abbey</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhys-ap-gruffydd">the Lord Rhys</a> died in 1197, his sons divided Deheubarth in bitter feuds. Its remnants came under Gwynedd's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-wales">Principality of Wales</a>, and its lands were absorbed by the English crown after 1283.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-deheubarth.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Deheubarth" width="320" height="421"><figcaption>Image: Owj20 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medieval_Wales.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>920 CE – 1197 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dinefwr</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hywel Dda, Rhys ap Tewdwr, Rhys ap Gruffydd</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Welsh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Deheubarth</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1058&amp;focus=kingdom-of-deheubarth" aria-label="Kingdom of Deheubarth on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4589 384 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Deheubarth lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4909 640L4894 640M4909 640L4910 602M4909 640L4970 663M4909 640L4924 638"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4894 640h0M4910 602h0M4970 663h0M4924 638h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4909 640h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4909 640h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dinefwr. <a href="/atlas?year=1058&amp;focus=kingdom-of-deheubarth">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
